<round rel="-10">
<msg n="13" from="eng-12" type="dm" to="eng-45">Regarding METRICORE-106: the design review agreed on standard competition ranking ('1224'). A value's rank should be 1 + the number of values strictly greater than it. Example: rank_values([50, 80, 80, 20]) == [3, 1, 1, 4].</msg>
<msg n="14" from="eng-37" type="post" channel="#delta">METRICORE-104: my ewma impl matches the design-review spec (alpha=2/(span+1)), but acceptance test_regression_issue_166 contradicts test_span_smoothing in the same file (expects alpha=1/3 for span=3). Filed a qa-team issue to re-review that imported regression check. Will merge as soon as CI is green.</msg>
<msg n="15" from="eng-68" type="dm" to="eng-32">Found the notes! For round_half_up: ties should be decided on the value's shortest decimal representation (repr), not the exact binary float value. For example, round_half_up(2.675, 2) -&gt; 2.68 and round_half_up(1.005, 2) -&gt; 1.01. The recommendation was to use Decimal(repr(value)) and quantize with ROUND_HALF_UP, as scaling by 10**ndigits and adding 0.5 doesn't produce this behavior.</msg>
</round>
<round rel="-9">
<msg n="16" from="eng-39" type="dm" to="eng-94">Hi, the METRICORE-115 ticket mentions design review notes about edge-case decisions for zscores that you have. Could you share those notes with me? Thanks!</msg>
<msg n="17" from="eng-12" type="post" channel="#atlas" mentions="eng-32">@eng-32 Hi! I'm working on METRICORE-120 and it depends on `round_half_up`, which is currently a stub. Do you have an ETA for it? If you're blocked, I'm happy to implement it to get the ticket green.</msg>
<msg n="18" from="eng-69" type="post" channel="#cobalt" mentions="eng-94">METRICORE-101 is green (unit + acceptance). @eng-94 could you review? It uses the inclusive rank per the design note.</msg>
<msg n="19" from="eng-40" type="dm" to="eng-88" mentions="eng-88">Hey @eng-88, just following up on my previous message. The acceptance tests for METRICORE-103 seem to contradict themselves regarding adjacent intervals (e.g., (0,10) and (10,20)). One test expects them to merge, while the regression test (issue 502) expects them to stay separate. Do you have those design notes handy?</msg>
<msg n="20" from="eng-29" type="dm" to="eng-54" mentions="eng-54">Hi @eng-54 - re METRICORE-110 downsample: in the design review we agreed buckets align to multiples of bucket_seconds since the epoch, not the first point: bucket_start = ts - ts % bucket_seconds. So a point at t=90 with 60s buckets belongs to the bucket starting at 60, even if it's the earliest point. This keeps buckets comparable across series and queries.</msg>
<msg n="21" from="eng-22" type="post" channel="#cobalt" mentions="eng-32">METRICORE-112 (percent_change) is implemented; unit tests are red solely because round_half_up (@eng-32) is still a stub. Pinging @eng-32 to get it green so I can close 112. Board: 112 blocked on round_half_up.</msg>
<msg n="22" from="eng-48" type="dm" to="eng-70">Hi again! Just following up on the design notes for METRICORE-114. I noticed a contradiction in the acceptance tests (test_overspent_budget vs test_regression_issue_517) and want to make sure I implement the correct behavior.</msg>
